│     "abstract": "OBJECTIVE Treatment of dyskinetic disorders, in general, and of tardive dyskinesia (TD), in         │
│ particular, is difficult. The opiate peptide enkephalin coexits with gamma aminobutyric acid in the projection       │
│ neurons of striatum forming the \"indirect\" pathway. Several lines of preclinical evidence implicate this           │
│ enkephalin-comediated pathway in the pathophysiology and therapeutics of dyskinesia. However, previous studies, most │
│ using relatively low doses of opioid antagonists, showed mixed results. The goal of the current study was to test    │
