│ imputation methods in two meta-analyses of antidepressants. RESULTS Two meta-analyses included 39 RCTs of fluoxetine │
│ (n = 3,681) and 25 RCTs of amitriptyline (n = 1,832), which had actually reported means and SDs of the Hamilton      │
│ Rating Scale for Depression. According to either of the two proposed imputation methods, the agreement between       │
