│ as a “dyskinesie facio-bucco-lingui-masticatrice”(BLM or orofacial syndrome).* The concept has evolved to include    │
│ nonrepetitive choreic and choreoathetoid movements of fingers, hands, and feet. It also includes choreoathetoid      │
│ movements of the legs and trunk. Tardive dystonia6 and tardive akathisia’may also be related to the TD complex.      │
│ Tardive dyskinesia must be differentiated from other neurological disorders such as Huntington’s chorea, Sydenham’s  │
│ chorea, drug-induced chorea, levodopa-induced dyskinesias, and the idiopathic and symptomatic dystonias. History of  │
